      "content": "Sorry, I should have realized. I'll paste the text below. \n\n[MANUSCRIPT EXCERPT: Section 3.2 - Statistical Validation. \"To account for nonlinear scaling in the neural-quantum interface, we utilized a standard linear regression model across the observed data points. While certain residuals suggested non-linearity, the overall trend remained statistically significant (p < 0.05), justifying the use of the linear approach for this preliminary study.\"]\n\n[REVIEWER 1: A groundbreaking piece of work. The implications for neuro-computation are massive. Recommend immediate publication.]\n\n[REVIEWER 2: I have serious concerns about the statistical framework. The authors use linear regression on data that clearly exhibits exponential growth patterns in the quantum flux measurements. This is a fundamental error; a linear model will significantly misrepresent the scaling relationship and could lead to false conclusions about stability.]\n\n[REVIEWER 3: The control groups are adequate, though I'd like to see more detail on the sensor calibration. Otherwise, the methodology is sound enough for a high-impact journal.]\n\nBased on these reviews and that excerpt from the methodology, is there any fundamental flaw here that would preclude publication?",
